==Enemy==
Cala Maria is a powerful enemy that has a very different attack than her [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant. To attack, she slams the ground three times in succession, dealing very high damage, enough to kill or severely damage most units. However, to balance this, she has Single Target with two knockbacks before death. Not many good attackers outrange her, which, despite her single target, still means that frail units will easily be in her reach, ready to be hit as soon as there is an opening.

Like other Angels, she is not considered a Floating enemy.

==Strategy==
Her weakness is that her three consecutive attacks are all Single Target, which means she can only hit up to three [[Cat Units]] per attack animation (the three frontmost units) in a stack of many. This allows your damage dealers to survive easily if protected by a horde of meatshields. The important thing is maintaining that horde, for a gap in the meatshield line might easily result in a precious backliner losing most, if not all of its health.

Cala Maria makes up for Single Target by delivering very high damage, causing cats with [[Resistant|resistance]] to [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemies, such as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|Guardian Gamereon]], to rarely be worth as much as a group of cheaper, one-off meatshields or [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]]. When paired with [[:Category:Area Attack Enemies|Area Attackers]] or even other [[:Category:Single Attack Enemies|Single Attackers]], (e.g., [[Berserkory]] in [[Steamed to Death]] and [[Capy]] in [[Drunken Backrub]]), however, tanking the damage might still be the better option, so don't rule out Ramen Cat if you see her! With the [[Heaven's Fruit]] maxed, a level 38 Ramen Cat has enough health to survive a full attack cycle from a 100% Cala Maria.

