==Trivia==
*Cala Maria may be based on the squid species [[wikipedia:Ancistroteuthis lichtensteinii|''Ancistroteuthis lichtensteinii'']], commonly known as the angel clubhook squid or simply angel squid.
*Like [[Calamary]], Cala Maria's name is a pun on the word ''calamari'', meaning fried squid.
*Cala Maria's description stating that she was sent by [[The Cat God (Special Cat)|The Cat God]] could be a nod to Christianity, originated from her name.
**It's unclear how Cat God could have sent Cala Maria, as [[Stories of Legend]] takes place before he was born. Note that Cala Maria's Japanese description doesn't mention Cat God at all, making this paradox specific to [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]].
***The existence of [[God (Special Cat)|God]] could potentially rectify this, since he is stated to transcend time and space.
**Cala Maria could also be a play on "Beata Maria", or Blessed Mary, the mother of Jesus.
*Her Japanese name, Ika Ten (イカ天), literally means "squid heaven" and is short for "ika tempura" (イカ天ぷら, squid tempura).
*The line "翼のイカれたエンジェル" (tsubasa no ikareta angel) in her Japanese description can be taken to mean either "squid-winged angel" or "crazy-winged angel", while also being a pun on the song "[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XmYKA_NRvEc Tsubasa no Oreta Angel]" (翼の折れたエンジェル, "Broken-Winged Angel") by [[wikipedia:ja:中村あゆみ|Ayumi Nakamura]].
*The term used to describe Cala Maria's attack in her Japanese description is 肩たたき ''katatataki'', meaning a shoulder massage performed by ''[[wikipedia:tapotement|tapotement]]'' (a massage technique involving rapid and repeated striking of the body).
**The Japanese names of [[Drunken Backrub]] (Drunk Massager) and [[Spa of Ascension]] (Ascension Spa Massage) directly allude to this.
*Since she's an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]], the first two digits of Cala Maria's 360,000 HP, 36,000 damage per hit and 36,000 damage per second may allude to the 36 holy [[wikipedia:Tzadikim Nistarim|Tzadikim Nistarim]] in Judaism.
*Cala Maria is the first enemy to have had multi-hit from the start rather than gaining it retroactively.
*Cala Maria and [[Heracrist (Enemy)|Heracrist]] are the only Angels to have single-target attacks.

